cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  eps-ground-rupture — interactive companion to Chiama et al. (2025)
message: >-
  This record identifies the software and the companion website. If you use the
  analyses or the data behind them, cite the paper under `preferred-citation`
  as well — and, for the data itself, the archives it comes from (DesignSafe-CI
  for the DEM experiments; the field compilations carry their own citations).
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/HarvardRC/eps-ground-rupture
url: https://harvardrc.github.io/eps-ground-rupture/
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline and companion website for the 2D distinct element
  method (DEM) surface-rupture analyses of Chiama et al. (2025). The pipeline
  cleans the published model outputs and field compilations into tidy Parquet,
  derives thirteen DuckDB views pinned by tests, and exports the CSV tables
  behind five interactive Tableau Public dashboards. The site documents what
  each dashboard answers, how every number is computed, and where each departs
  from the printed figures.
keywords:
  - earthquake
  - surface rupture
  - distinct element method
  - fault displacement hazard
  - scarp morphology
  - reproducible research
